# The name map unit 10E applied (decision 1349 settles 10D's draft): kerf-rename's map for the kernel's four assemblies.
# Drafted by `kerf-rename draft` (unit 10D) with the seed docs/api/kerf-seed.map, finished by `api-classify.cs
# --finish-map`, then settled in 10E: decision 1349's names (57: `2D`/`3D` only where both exist, so gp_Cone, gp_Cylinder,
# gp_Sphere, gp_Torus and gp_Ax3 lose theirs; Plane3D keeps its suffix, Plane being System.Numerics's), interfaces
# prefixed I, exceptions ending in Exception, and the clashes the tool and api-classify found ('10E' in the note).
# Types marked 'public API (10D)' take the names of the API reviews in docs/api; 'engine (10D)' the engine's namespaces;
# 'draft' the drafter's systematic names. Removed types (NCollection, TCollection, PackedList…) have no entries: they
# keep their OCCT names in the namespace Occt until 10J (decision 1349, 58).
#
# The maps as applied, with a keep line for every rename the tool dropped, are in docs/api/applied: those, not this
# file, say what each OCCT name became. Ids are Roslyn's documentation comment ids. Format: kerf-rename/README.md.

